.\" Manual page for bogenplan. @VERSION@ is filled in by build-deb.sh.
.\"
.\" Author: David M. Anderson
.\" Built with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic)
.TH BOGENPLAN 1 "2026\-11\-08" "bogenplan @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bogenplan \- a calendar laid out on the Sun's arc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bogenplan
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.RB [ \-\-date
.IR YYYY\-MM\-DD ]
.RB [ \-\-zoom
.IR points ]
.RI [ file.ics " | " webcal://address ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Bogenplan
shows the calendars kept on iCloud or another CalDAV server in Bogenzeit.
Each day runs from one solar midnight to the next and holds 400 spans, with
sunrise at 100, solar noon at 200 and sunset at 300, so daylight always fills
the middle half of the column and the events move with the seasons.
.PP
Pressing and holding an empty part of a day shows the reading at that point;
holding still until the line turns gold and letting go sets a moment there, a
zero\-length event with an alert at its start, added to the calendar chosen in
Settings. Double\-clicking does the same at once.
.PP
Opening an iCalendar file, from the command line or as the desktop's calendar
application, shows its events and adds them to a calendar of your choosing.
An invitation is saved as your own copy without its organizer and attendees,
so nothing is sent to the organizer. An event already in your calendars with
the same UID is replaced, and a cancellation removes it. When Bogenplan is
already open, the file goes to that window.
.PP
Opening a
.B webcal://
address asks to subscribe to that calendar. A subscribed calendar is shown
read\-only beside the others and fetched from its publisher over HTTPS at most
once an hour. Settings also subscribes by address, recolors a subscription and
removes it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Show a sample week in Houston instead of the calendars signed in.
.TP
.BI \-\-date " YYYY\-MM\-DD"
Open on this date rather than today.
.TP
.BI \-\-zoom " points"
Open with this many points per span.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bogenplan/settings.json
Scale, precision, hidden calendars, the calendar for moments and the place.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/bogenplan/calendars.json
The events last fetched, readable only by the user.
.PP
Passwords are kept in the desktop keyring under the attribute
.BR service=bogenplan ,
with
.B server
and
.B username
beside it. The address of each calendar subscribed in Bogenplan is kept under
.BR service=bogenplan\-feed ,
with
.B feed
and
.B color
beside it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns success when the window has been closed. A non\-zero status means the
window could not be created at all: no display, or no usable graphics driver.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bz (1)
.SH AUTHOR
David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>
